# Quote form delivery — set these in Vercel project settings AND locally in
# .env.local (which is gitignored). Names only here, never real values.
#
# DEPLOY ORDER MATTERS: these must exist in Vercel BEFORE the code that uses
# them ships. With none of them set, every channel skips, /api/contact
# correctly concludes nothing was delivered, and every submission returns 502.
# That is the failure rule working as designed — but it turns a working form
# into a broken one.

# --- Telegram: the primary alert -------------------------------------------
# The owner does not reliably check email, which is the entire reason this
# exists. Telegram pushes and keeps an unread badge until he opens it.
#
# 1. Message @BotFather in Telegram, /newbot, copy the token here.
# 2. The owner installs Telegram and sends the bot any message — a bot cannot
#    open a conversation first, so this step is required.
# 3. Read the chat id from:
#    https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
#    → result[0].message.chat.id
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Resend: the durable record + the customer confirmation -----------------
# Free tier covers far more than this site sends.
#
# The customer-facing email also needs acadiapools.com verified in Resend
# (DKIM + SPF records, added at GoDaddy — the domain has no MX records, so
# nothing collides). Until it verifies, Resend can only send from
# onboarding@resend.dev, which is fine for the owner's internal copy but must
# not be used for the customer confirmation — it reads as phishing to someone
# who just handed over their home address.
RESEND_API_KEY=
